# Retire policy 2026-11-20: still in production in 2026 with no announced end; retire dates commented out. Revisit when an end is announced.
# Land Rover Discovery 5 five-door, 2017 onwards.
#
# The fifth Discovery: the aluminium monocoque, the smooth rounded body, the
# clamshell bonnet and the offset rear plate. The five-door is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land_Rover_Discovery
#
# Dimensions 4.956-4.970 x 2.000 m (body; 2.073 with mirrors folded) x
# 1.888 m, wheelbase 2.923 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is the side profile; the front and rear
# three-quarters show the lamps, grille and tailgate. The notes record the
# short-read nose caused by the camera angle.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the 2017 model year UK Discovery brochure: Fuji White,
# Santorini Black, Indus Silver and Loire Blue. Weights 12, 10, 10, 8,
# total 40, provisional.
#
# Speed 210 km/h. Comfort 95/473, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 95. Class 3.
# Dates are road presence: 2017 intro, retire dates commented out (still in production in 2026).
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/land-rover-discovery-5.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/land-rover-discovery-5.dae. References:
# citycars/references/land-rover-discovery-5/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true profile, so the flank is estimated. The
# rear overhang and tail are squarer than the photograph's rounded tail, the
# quarter glass is a rectangular panel and the arch cladding is a flat ribbon.
# At 128 px the rising belt, floating roof and horizontal tail lamps read as a
# Discovery 5, though the floating roof is weakly expressed at this size.


obj=citycar
name=LandRoverDiscovery5(FujiWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=2017
intro_month=4
#retire_year=2041
#retire_month=6
speed=210
class=3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=95
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=473

